# Synthetic carrier for 0x47fe0b (bf_47fe0b): a multiplayer player resigning while a field battle runs (0x49cf20 calls it
# when DAT_0057c8fc == 2) — no scenario resigns mid-battle. field-orders f3000 = the siege battle (48 units; owners on
# +0x2c, DAT_005544ac). Every call: units of owner p get men +0x174 = 0, state +5 = 2, DAT_00554489 = 0, cue 13; the loop
# index DAT_0053e8f8 ends at 81 (the return = 432 * 80 unless record 80 matched: the cue's EAX). Owners here: 2 (u1..24)
# and 1 (u25..48). 0x101 first: retail compares the zero-extended owner byte with the whole int (no match; a byte
# compare would kill side 1).
